// FLOWS
// auth-code-par: Issuance — authorization code flow with PAR. Issuer-initiated issuance on one device. The Wallet authenticates with its Wallet Instance Attestation at the PAR and token endpoints, binds the access token with DPoP, fetches a nonce, obtains a key attestation bound to that nonce from its Wallet Provider, and proves key possession with a jwt proof that carries the key attestation.
//   1 Wallet Provider → Wallet Unit: Wallet Instance Attestation → WalletInstanceAttestation
//   2 Credential Issuer → Wallet Unit: Credential Offer → Offer
//   3 Wallet Unit → Credential Issuer: GET /.well-known/openid-credential-issuer → Metadata
//   4 Wallet Unit: validate signed metadata (x5c)
//   5 Wallet Unit → Authorization Server: GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server → AsMetadata
//   6 Wallet Unit → Authorization Server: POST /par → ParRequest
//   7 Authorization Server: validate PAR request
//   7.1 Authorization Server: verify WIA
//   7.2 Authorization Server: verify WIA PoP
//   7.3 Authorization Server: PKCE, scope, redirect_uri
//   8 Authorization Server → Wallet Unit: 201 request_uri → ParResponse
//   9 Wallet Unit → Authorization Server: GET /authorize (via browser) → AuthorizationRequest
//   10 Authorization Server: authenticate user, consent
//   11 Authorization Server → Wallet Unit: 302 code, iss → AuthorizationResponse
//   12 Wallet Unit: check state + iss
//   13 Wallet Unit → Authorization Server: POST /token → TokenRequest
//   14 Authorization Server: validate token request
//   14.1 Authorization Server: verify WIA
//   14.2 Authorization Server: verify WIA PoP
//   14.3 Authorization Server: verify DPoP proof
//   14.4 Authorization Server: code + code_verifier (PKCE)
//   15 Authorization Server → Wallet Unit: DPoP access token → TokenResponse
//   16 Wallet Unit → Credential Issuer: POST /nonce → NonceRequest
//   17 Credential Issuer → Wallet Unit: c_nonce → NonceResponse
//   18 Wallet Unit → Wallet Provider: request key attestation (c_nonce) → KeyAttestation
//   19 Wallet Provider → Wallet Unit: key attestation → KeyAttestation
//   20 Wallet Unit → Credential Issuer: POST /credential → CredentialRequest
//   21 Credential Issuer: validate credential request
//   21.1 Credential Issuer: access token + DPoP (ath, jkt)
//   21.2 Credential Issuer: credential configuration + proofs
//   21.3 Credential Issuer: verify key attestation
//   21.4 Credential Issuer: verify key proof (nonce, aud)
//   22 Credential Issuer: create and sign credentials
//   22.1 Credential Issuer: one credential per attested key
//   22.2 Credential Issuer: sign SD-JWT VC (x5c)
//   23 Credential Issuer → Wallet Unit: credentials → CredentialResponse
//   24 Wallet Unit → Credential Issuer: POST /notification → NotificationRequest
//   25 Credential Issuer → Wallet Unit: 204
// pre-auth: Issuance — pre-authorized code flow, cross device. The user is authenticated on the issuer's website and scans a QR code with the wallet on a second device. The offer carries a pre-authorized code; a transaction code sent on a separate channel can bind it to the user. By the binding rules the token request still carries the WIA (CIR TR-WIA-3 does not depend on the grant). The example messages are recorded from a d-you issuance (IDGo 81, 2026-10-22): no transaction code, no WIA and no key attestation, encrypted Credential Request and Response, no notification endpoint.
//   1 Wallet Provider → Wallet Unit: Wallet Instance Attestation → WalletInstanceAttestation
//   2 Credential Issuer → Wallet Unit: QR code with credential_offer_uri → Offer
//   3 Wallet Unit → Credential Issuer: GET credential_offer_uri → OfferFetch
//   4 Credential Issuer → Wallet Unit: Transaction Code (SMS, e-mail)
//   5 Wallet Unit → Credential Issuer: GET /.well-known/openid-credential-issuer → Metadata
//   6 Wallet Unit: validate signed metadata (x5c)
//   7 Wallet Unit → Authorization Server: GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server → AsMetadata
//   8 Wallet Unit → Authorization Server: POST /token (pre-authorized code) → TokenRequest
//   9 Authorization Server: validate token request
//   9.1 Authorization Server: verify WIA
//   9.2 Authorization Server: verify WIA PoP
//   9.3 Authorization Server: verify DPoP proof
//   9.4 Authorization Server: pre-authorized_code + tx_code
//   10 Authorization Server → Wallet Unit: DPoP access token → TokenResponse
//   11 Wallet Unit → Credential Issuer: POST /nonce → NonceRequest
//   12 Credential Issuer → Wallet Unit: c_nonce → NonceResponse
//   13 Wallet Unit → Wallet Provider: request key attestation (c_nonce) → KeyAttestation
//   14 Wallet Provider → Wallet Unit: key attestation → KeyAttestation
//   15 Wallet Unit → Credential Issuer: POST /credential → CredentialRequest
//   16 Credential Issuer: validate credential request
//   16.1 Credential Issuer: access token + DPoP (ath, jkt)
//   16.2 Credential Issuer: credential configuration + proofs
//   16.3 Credential Issuer: verify key attestation
//   16.4 Credential Issuer: verify key proof (nonce, aud)
//   17 Credential Issuer: create and sign credentials
//   17.1 Credential Issuer: one credential per attested key
//   17.2 Credential Issuer: sign SD-JWT VC (x5c)
